Runtime fixes from the God of War II port (cxldsakeb, DaniSBR1; github.com/DaniSBR1/PS2Recomp branch godofwar2, built on
the same Waffle565 runtime as Tobiichi), the ones its notes mark valid for God of War, in its commit order:
8a4abab d0b6162 2b20dc4 eb5657e 1faaa0e 75c0c1d c012422 1d9f4b6 261fb44 (GS HW renderer: channel shuffles ending on a
fractional pixel, Z16 shuffle source, reinterpreted reads of scaled targets, Z-format sprites clearing GL depth, bloom
reads at internal scale (the "ghost"), CLAMP to TW x TH, point-sampled scaled targets, sprite edges like the GS,
whole particles, GOW_ANISO=2..16 anisotropic filtering); 9499406 (the runtime's RPC/TLS/boot-mode guest pools moved
from 0x01F00000 to the top of the private heap, out of the game's heap); 6d3379b (scratchpad DMA interleave mode);
ac9dfaf (PSS audio to the stream type the game registered); e347878 (memory card file kept open between page
writes); df2a082 (IOP sysclib strtok / thbase GetSystemTimeLow, warning for unhandled kernel imports).
Left out: 5b1a25a (SetupThread argc/argv: God of War then loads its IRX as cdrom0:\...;1 and hangs at boot without
the IOP path changes of 9ccffe1). Measured with 06 and 07 on the ship (Xeon E5-2666 v3, RX 580, 2x): image correct,
combat 44-50 -> 55-60 fps.

